{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNWWiring","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookGNWWiring","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTCornerListConnection","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaProd"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaFactProd_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaFactProd_cast","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L163-L177","doc":"**`betaFactProd` as `∏ βᵢ!`.** `(betaFactProd l : ℚ) = ∏_{i<k} (βᵢ)!`. Each factor depends only on\n`l[i]` and the drop *length* `k−1−i`, so under `removeCorner = l.set c (l[c]−1)` only factor `c` changes\n(the factorial side of the per-corner ratio). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNatVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNatVal","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L160-L161","doc":"The `ℕ`-valued β-number `βᵢ = l[i] + (k−1−i)` (= `betaNat l i` as a natural). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaProdGap_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaProdGap_cast","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L144-L158","doc":"**`betaProdGap` as the Vandermonde double-product.** `(betaProdGap l : ℚ) = ∏_{i<k} ∏_{i<j}(βᵢ−βⱼ)`,\nassembling the per-row casts. This is `∏_{i<j}(βᵢ − βⱼ)` organised by lower-triangular column `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaGapProd_row_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaGapProd_row_cast","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L124-L142","doc":"**Per-row Vandermonde factor.** The corpus' recursive gap factor at row `i` is the column\n`∏_{i<j}(βᵢ − βⱼ)` of the Vandermonde: `betaGapProd (l[i]) (l.drop (i+1)) = ∏_{m<k−1−i}(βᵢ − β_{i+1+m})`\n(reindex `j = i+1+m`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec_eq_betaNat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec_eq_betaNat","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L121-L122","doc":"`betaVec` is `betaNat` restricted to `Fin k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaNat","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L116-L119","doc":"The `ℕ`-indexed β-value `βᵢ = l[i] + (k−1−i)` (no `Fin` bound), for stating Vandermonde products\nover `range`. Agrees with `betaVec` on valid indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaGapProd_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaGapProd_cast","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L95-L114","doc":"**`betaGapProd` as an explicit ℚ product.** `(betaGapProd a t : ℚ) = ∏_{m<|t|} (a + 1 + m − t[m])`\n— each factor is cast-safe because the tail entries are `≤ a`.  This identifies the corpus' recursive\nVandermonde factor `betaGapProd (l[i]) (l.drop (i+1))` with `∏_{j>i}(βᵢ − βⱼ)` (factor `m` is\n`l[i] + (m+1) − l[i+1+m] = βᵢ − β_{i+1+m}`), the keystone for the per-corner hook ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_betaVec_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_betaVec_sub","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L83-L89","doc":"**`betaLagrange`'s RHS is `sz l`.** `∑ⱼ βⱼ − C(k,2) = sz l`, so the β-Lagrange identity evaluates\nto the cell count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_shift_triangular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_shift_triangular","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L73-L81","doc":"`∑_{i : Fin k} (k − 1 − i) = C(k,2)` — the staircase shifts sum to the triangular number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_getD","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L61-L71","doc":"`∑_{i : Fin k} (l[i] : ℚ) = sz l` — the β-vector's length part sums to the cell count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec_injective","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L56-L59","doc":"**The β-vector has distinct entries** (strictly antitone ⟹ injective). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec_strictAnti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec_strictAnti","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L39-L54","doc":"**The β-vector is strictly antitone**: `i < i'` gives `βᵢ > β_{i'}` — the row length is weakly\ndecreasing while the staircase shift `k−1−i` strictly decreases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec_eq_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec_eq_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L34-L37","doc":"For a weakly-decreasing shape, `βᵢ` is an integer (a cast `ℕ`): `l[i] + (k−1−i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaVec","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookGNWWiring.lean#L30-L32","doc":"The β-vector of a shape `l`: `βᵢ = l[i] + (k − 1 − i)` over `ℚ`, where `k = l.length`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}